    "created_at": "2024-08-19T16:42:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-19T16:42:58Z",
    "body": "Right, it's currently just under the undefined behavior umbrella of [RFC 9110 Error Handling](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-2.4):\r\n> Unless noted otherwise, a recipient **MAY** attempt to recover a usable protocol element from an invalid construct… For example, a Web browser might wish to transparently recover from a response where the <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#field.location\">Location</a> header field doesn't parse according to the ABNF",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
